Disables Jekyll processing on GitHub Pages.

Without this file Pages runs the repo through Jekyll, which skips any file or
directory whose name starts with an underscore. That silently dropped the whole
of images/_derived/ from the published site: every .thumb.webp / .md.webp /
.poster.webp / .opt.mp4 returned 404 while the original images served fine, so
the site fell back to full-size originals (js/site/media.js setImg onerror) and
the console filled with 404s.

Keep this file. It must stay at the repo root, and its contents don't matter.
